1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:06,456
My living room wall just grew a glowing green exit door, and my dog refuses to look at it.

2
00:00:06,756 --> 00:00:13,164
I told myself it was a glitch, a faulty projection from the street lamps outside my downtown window.

3
00:00:13,464 --> 00:00:19,536
Except I live on the fortieth floor, and there is no balcony out there for a door to lead to.

4
00:00:19,836 --> 00:00:26,748
My hands shook as I reached out, my fingers wrapping around the cold brass handle that shouldn't exist.

5
00:00:27,048 --> 00:00:33,960
I pulled it open, expecting brick or empty air, but found a blinding white light instead.

6
00:00:34,260 --> 00:00:42,204
Stepping through, the city noise vanished, replaced by the soft hum of heavy machinery and cooling fans.

7
00:00:42,504 --> 00:00:48,576
Then I looked back at the door I just walked through and saw my entire living room framed inside it.

8
00:00:48,876 --> 00:00:55,356
My dog was still sitting there, staring right at the back of the frame, wagging his tail at the watchers.

9
00:00:55,656 --> 00:01:03,648
Giant hands reached down from the ceiling above the lab, holding a remote control and laughing at my confusion.

10
00:01:03,948 --> 00:01:09,204
If this is their entertainment, what is playing on the walls of the room they are sitting in right now?
